expression: help
---
Read-only command-line client for the HookahWork CRM API.

hw only reads: every command is a GET request, plus the two non-mutating POSTs the API
needs for logging in and for searching a client. Nothing in the CRM is created, changed
or deleted.

Usage: hw [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  ref          Reference data: settings, tables, payment methods, employees, services, bonus levels
  product      Products and product categories
  storage      Storages and purchases
  client       Clients: list, groups, visit history, lookup
  booking      Bookings: daily list, timetable, single booking, device bookings
  sale         Sales at tables or over a business day
  hookah       Hookahs served at tables or over a business day
  report       Daily reports: expenses, credits, bonus points
  analytics    Period summaries of hookahs and sales
  menu         Public electronic menu (works without a token)
  api          Send a raw GET request to any API path
  auth         Log in and manage the stored API token
  config       Inspect and manage configuration profiles
  completions  Print a shell completion script
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global Options:
  -v, --verbose...
          Increase logging verbosity (-v, -vv, -vvv); logs go to stderr

  -q, --quiet
          Print only errors to stderr: no hints, no warnings

      --config <PATH>
          Configuration file [default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hw/config.toml or ~/.config/hw/config.toml]
          
          [env: HW_CONFIG=]

  -p, --profile <NAME>
          Profile from the configuration file to use
          
          [env: HW_PROFILE=]

      --crm <CRM>
          CRM to talk to: subdomain (demo), host (demo.hookah.work) or base URL
          
          [env: HW_CRM=]

  -F, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - console: Tables and `key: value` lines for people
          - json:    Pretty-printed JSON
          - toon:    TOON, a compact JSON encoding for LLMs
          - toml:    TOML (a top-level list is wrapped as `items`)
          - csv:     CSV with a header row
          
          [default: console]

      --no-color
          Disable colored output (NO_COLOR is honoured too)

      --no-pager
          Do not page console output (also HW_NO_PAGER=1)

      --jq <EXPR>
          Filter the JSON result with a jq expression before formatting

      --template <TPL>
          Render the result with a minijinja template instead of --format

      --retries <N>
          Retries for rate limiting (429), server errors (5xx) and network failures; 0 disables
          
          [default: 3]

Getting started:
  hw auth login
  hw booking list --date today
  hw product list --search чай -F json

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 runtime/API/network error, 2 not found, 3 configuration error,
4 authentication error, 5 invalid input.
